{"type":"click","text":"Approach B: Role-Augmented Existing Pages Recommended\nNo new hub. Instead, existing pages (resume, roles, apply, interview, skills) are each \"role-aware\" — they detect the active role and show role-specific context inline. Roles are managed from a compact settings panel or a drawer.\n\nRoles page becomes richer: grid of role cards with overlay previews inline\nResume builder: role selector dropdown in the header (\"Building for: [BA ▾]\")\nApply flow: same recommended-with-preview as A\nInterview: same contextual prompts as A\nSkills module: same tabs + sidebar as A\nApplications: same primary + variant model as A\nNew: \"Role Panel\" drawer (accessed from any page) — add/edit/swap active role\n\nOverlay architecture: Same separate table model. Role panel is a global UI element (like a notification drawer) accessible from any page.\nTradeoff: More complex distributed UX (role context appears in many places). But users never leave their current page to manage roles. Higher engineering complexity — role context needs to flow through more components.","choice":"b","id":null,"timestamp":1776195238899}
